  they help in observing and  troubleshooting the issues  that may occur due to variation in long  time  in automation testing weight commands  direct the test execution to pause for a  certain  length of time before moving on to the  next step  there are two types of weight commands  they are the implicit weight and the  explicit weight  first we will learn the implicit weight  implicit weights  tell the web driver to wait for a  certain amount of time before it throws  an exception  once we set the time webdriver will wait  for the element based on the time  we set before it throws an exception the  default setting is  zero we need to set some wait time to  make  webdriver to wait for a required time  now we will learn about the explicit  weight the explicit to weight in  selenium is used to tell the web driver  to wait for a certain condition or  maximum time exceeded before throwing an  exception  that is the element not a visible  exception  moving on to the next question  what is the biggest disadvantage of  implicit  weight the main disadvantage of the  implicit weight is that it slows down  the test performance  webdriver will wait for some specific  amount of time before it throws an  exception  for example if you set the waiting time  to be 10 seconds  and the elements appear in the dom in 11  seconds  your test will fail because you told to  wait  for a maximum of 10 seconds only  now moving on to the next question what  are the type of  navigation commands so the different  types of navigation commands are  the first one driver dot navigate  to url this navigates to the provided  url  then comes driver.navigate.refresh  this method refreshes the current page  the third command  is the driver.navigate.forward this  method  does the same operation as clicking on  forward button  of any browser it neither accepts nor  returns anything  last navigation command is the  driver.navigate.pack  this method does the same operation as  clicking on the  back button of any browser it neither  accepts  nor returns anything moving on to the  next question  what is meant by same origin policy and  how is it handled same origin policy is  a feature  taken for security purposes  according to this policy a web browser  enables the access of scripts  from one web page to the other if both  the pages have the same origin  the origin policy protects a malicious  script on  one page to access sensitive data on  another  followed by this we have the next  question what is salinas and how  is it classified salinas is a set of  selenium commands which are used to test  your web application  testers can test the broken links the  existence of some objects on the ui  ajax functionality alerts on window  list options and a lot more using  cylinders  selenium commands tells the selenium  automation engine to perform certain  tasks  cylinders can be classified into a set  of three types of commands  which are action accessors and  assertions moving ahead we have the 35th  question what is the difference between  driver.close method  and driver.quit method so the answer for  this question  is the driver.close command is used to  close the current browser window  if there are multiple windows open on  the screen then  the one on focus will be closed whereas  the driver.quit command is also used for  the same purpose  if there are multiple browser windows  open on the screen  then the command closes all of them at  once  moving ahead we have the advanced level  of interview questions  now we are done with the intermediate  level of selenium interview questions  let's now buckle up a little more and  learn the advanced level of interview  questions  the first question in this category is  how do you type  text in an input box using selenium  the method used to type text in input  boxes is  send keys the send keys method allows  typing automatically into an editable  field during the execution of  any tests these fields are web elements  that can be identified using locators  like  element id name class name  etc now moving on to the next question  how to click on a hyperlink in selenium  the command used to click on the  hyperlink uses  link text to find the element the  command finds the element using  linked text and then clicks on the  element  where after the user would be redirected  to the corresponding page  you can find the syntax of the command  on the screen  moving on to the next question how to  scroll down a page using  javascript the method used to scroll  down to a page is scroll by we can see  the syntaxes of a set of commands the  first syntax that is the execute script  here  is the general syntax for scroll by  command then the second syntax of  javascript executor is  create a javascript object then the  third syntax  driver.get is the syntax of launching  the desired application  then the last syntax that is the js  dot execute script is for the scroll  down to the desired location  moving forward we have the next question  what is the way of typing in a text box  without using send keys the text can be  entered into a text box  by using javascript executor the  commands that could be used  for the process can be seen on the  screen you can use  javascript executor and jse dot  execute script for the work to be done  now moving forward we have the next  question how to select a value from a  drop down in selenium web driver  for selecting and deselecting from a  drop down in selenium web driver  select class is used the objects of  select type can be initialized by  passing  the drop down web element as a parameter  to its constructor  the syntax of the commands can be seen  on the screen  the web element test drop command and  the command to select the drop down  here the web driver offers three ways to  select  from a drop down box the first way is to  select a buy index that is the selection  is based on index starting from zero  then comes select by value that is  selection based on value  the last way is select by visual text  that is selection of option that  displays text matching  the given argument the next question is  what is the use of switch to command the  answer for this question is  the switch to command is used to switch  between windows  frames or pop-ups within the application  every window instantiated by the  webdriver is given a unique alphanumeric  value called  window handle we can see the syntax of  commands on the screen  the first command that is the string  handle command is used to get the window  handle  of the window you wish to switch to and  then  the driver dot switch to command is used  to switch to  the desired window the next question is  what is meant by object repository in  selenium webdriver  an object repository is a common storage  location for all  objects if we talk in the context of  selenium webdriver  these objects would typically be the  locators used to identify  web elements uniquely for example if  there is a chance  in one web elements locator value then  only the object repository  has to be changed instead of all the  test cases  the object repositories have to be built  in selenium webdriver  using the key value pair approach the  two types of object repositories  may be created in selenium webdriver are  the  first one object repository using  properties file and the next one  object repository in xml moving ahead we  have the 43rd question  how to upload a file in selenium web  driver  to upload a file in selenium webdriver  the send keys or robot class method  are used the initial step is to first  locate the text box and then set the  file path using send keys method and  click on submit  the syntax for the command can be seen  on the screen  the first syntax of the web element  command is used to locate  the browse button then the second syntax  of the browse dot  send keys is used to pass the file path  to  be uploaded using send keys method  moving on to the next question  what is the way to set browser window  size in selenium  so the answer for this question is the  window size can be maximized  set or resized to maximize the window we  use the  dot driver.manage.window.max method or  command  and then to set the window size we can  use  dimension d is equals to new dimension  where in the brackets we give the  dimensions we want to set  the size now moving on to the next  question how can you debug test and  selenium ide  the steps to debug the test and selenium  ide are  the first step is to insert a breakpoint  from the place you want to execute your  test  then execute the text case after the  test case has started executing  the execution will pass at the  breakpoint then  click on the blue button with the next  statement to continue and finally  click on the run button to execute all  the commands  moving ahead we have the next question  how to insert a breakpoint in selenium  ide  the steps to insert a breakpoint in  selenium ide are  the first step is to go into the  selenium ide  right click on the command and select  toggle breakpoint  then select the command and press the b  key on the keyboard  pause that to clear the breakpoint press  b  key again and multiple breakpoints can  be set up in the selenium ide  moving forward we have the next question  what is a pause on  an exception in selenium ide so the  answer for this question  is the pause on an exception as a  feature  that is used to handle exceptions in  selenium ide  the feature can be used by clicking on  the pause button on the right  top corner of the ide window the  execution stops when an exception is  encountered  and the script enters to the debug mode  so the entire test  does not fail and the error can be  resolved  moving forward we have the 48th question  what can result in the failure of  selenium ide  so the answer for this question is  selenium ide is one of the most  accessible record and play tools in the  selenium tool suit  which requires no particular setup the  selenium ide  comes with a very rich set of commands  powered by surnase and  allows us to record and test different  web application  interactions with the browser but then  there are certain times when the  selenium ide might  fail some of those instances are when  selenium cannot locate the element  if the locator has changed then one more  such instance is when the element to be  accessed cannot be found on the web page  and operation is timed out  and one more case is when the element  being tried  to access is not created  for finding if the link is broken or  working fine we use the driver.get  method  when we use driver.getmethod to navigate  to a url  it will respond with a status of 200  okay  200 ok denotes that the link is working  and it has been obtained if any other  status is obtained then it indicates  that the link  is broken some of the http status quotes  are  200 that indicates it's a valid link 4.4  indicates link not found 400 indicates  bad request 4.1 indicates unauthorized  and finally 500 that indicates internal  error and now we are at the last  question  how to login to any site if it is  showing an authentication pop-up  for user name and password so the answer  for this question is  to handle authentication pop-ups we need  to verify its appearance  and then handle them using an explicit  weight command  the syntax of the explicit weight  command to be used is on the screen that  is  the first syntax webdriver weight syntax  the second syntax is the alert alert  equals to weight dot  until refers to the use of alert class  to verify the alert  and the last syntax is alert dot  authenticate that is there to provide  the credentials after the verification  in the previous step  and this is all for this session i hope  that after going through these  selenium interview questions you would  have understood what kind of  questions can be asked in your interview  and how you could approach them  in the best possible manner signing off  on this note subscribe to our channel  and stay tuned for more from simply  learn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel  and click here to watch similar videos  turn it up and get certified  click here
 

